@startuml
title ExitPass POS Server Context and Authority Boundary

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor "Finance / audit /\ncompliance" as Finance

rectangle "Payment channels / terminals" #F7FAFF {
    component "WebPay" as WebPay
    component "APM" as APM
    component "Cashier POS" as Cashier
    component "EC Device /\nContinuity Terminal" as EC
    component "Operator-assisted\npayment" as Operator
}

component "Payment Orchestrator\nprovider outcome verification" as Orchestrator
component "Central PMS\npayment finality + ExitAuthorization" as PMS
component "Site POS Server\nfiscal issuance + reporting" as POS
component "Gate Integration /\nExitAuthorization consumer" as Gate
component "Vendor PMS /\nHikCentral" as Vendor
database "BIR reporting outputs\nSI, X/Z, BIR Summary,\nAnnex E, EJ, POSLog" as BIR

WebPay --> Orchestrator : payment flow
APM --> Orchestrator : payment flow
Cashier --> Orchestrator : payment flow
EC --> Orchestrator : continuity payment flow
Operator --> Orchestrator : assisted payment flow

Orchestrator --> PMS : verified provider outcome
PMS --> POS : request SI issuance\nfor resolved Site
POS --> PMS : SI identity/status,\ndigital SI URL if applicable
PMS --> Gate : ExitAuthorization
PMS --> Vendor : synchronization only
Vendor --> PMS : acknowledgment/status
POS --> BIR : fiscal reports/exports
Finance --> POS : audit/report review

note bottom of PMS
Central PMS owns payment finality,
PaymentAttempt, PaymentConfirmation,
site resolution, and ExitAuthorization.
end note

note bottom of POS
POS Server owns fiscal issuance,
fiscal counters, reports, EJ, POSLog,
exports, audit, retention, and recovery.
It does not issue ExitAuthorization.
end note

@enduml
